# RULE: CSS Modules Naming

Applies to all renderer `*.module.css` and their TS/TSX consumers.

## CSS (`*.module.css`)

- Class selectors: **kebab-case** — `.row-panel`, `.nav-button-active`.
- Modifiers: hyphen-separated — `.state-indicator-positive`, not `.stateIndicator_positive`.
- Single-word classes are allowed — `.panel`, `.rail`.

## TypeScript / TSX

- Access exported classes with **dot notation** — `styles.rowPanel`.
- Forbidden: `styles["rowPanel"]`, `` styles[`rowPanel_${x}`] ``.
- Dynamic variants: `Record<Variant, string>` map bound to `styles.*` keys.

## Build

- Vite `css.modules.localsConvention: "camelCase"` in `electron.vite.config.ts`.
- `.row-panel` in CSS exports as `styles.rowPanel`.

## Lint

- ESLint: `@typescript-eslint/dot-notation`, `no-restricted-syntax` on `styles` / `*Styles`.
- Stylelint: `selector-class-pattern` on `src/**/*.module.css` (`npm run lint:css`).
